  "id": "10504_hodoku",
  "headword": "ほどく",
  "reading": "ほどく",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to untie, to undo",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to untie, to undo, to unfasten",
      "explanation": "To release something that has been tied, knotted, or fastened."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "10504_hodoku_ex1",
      "japanese": "{紐|ひも}をほどく。",
      "english": "To untie a string.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "10504_hodoku_ex2",
      "japanese": "{靴|くつ}の{紐|ひも}をほどいてから{脱|ぬ}いだ。",
      "english": "I untied my shoelaces before taking off my shoes.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "10504_hodoku_ex3",
      "japanese": "プレゼントのリボンをほどくのがもったいなかった。",
      "english": "It felt like a waste to untie the ribbon on the present.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "CONJUGATION (godan-ku):\n- Negative: ほどかない\n- Te-form: ほどいて\n- Past: ほどいた\n- Passive: ほどかれる\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\nTransitive. The intransitive counterpart is ほどける (to come untied).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {結|むす}び{目|め}をほどく: to undo a knot\n- {紐|ひも}をほどく: to untie a string\n- {帯|おび}をほどく: to undo an obi sash\n- {包|つつ}みをほどく: to unwrap a package",
